    "suggested_action": "human_review",
    "reason": "The English lemma 'tone' has multiple common meanings, including sound quality (e.g., musical tone), color shade, and manner of speaking. The Japanese expression '語気' (goki) specifically refers to the 'tone of voice' or 'manner of speaking'. It does not cover other common meanings of 'tone' such as musical tone (音色 - neiro) or color tone (色調 - shikichou). Therefore, '語気' is semantically narrower than the English 'tone'. A general learner looking up 'tone' might expect a broader term or be confused if they were thinking of other common meanings.",
